/-!
# Paper A (lock v12), lane `owner:a-eth-2`, segments 3-4, square variant on route B

Lock v12 `sections/06-reduction.tex:111-117`: "The conclusion also holds when the inputs are
square matrices of power-of-two side length." Proof, `:142-147`: "To obtain a square
power-of-two table, let $S$ be the least power of two at least $m_Y$, and repeat rows and
columns until both dimensions are $S$. ... the leading constant in \cref{eq:quantitative-size}
is unchanged."

Route B with the estimator hypothesis only on square power-of-two words (`EstimatesGrowingSelSq`,
verbatim from a-eth-owner-1 `AEthClass`): the header word is `natField (2·budget + k) ++ mwSqOf b`
(the square word of the printed table, a-decider-owner-2 `mwSqOf`, copied in `E2SqCore`); the
gap at the square word is the admitted `Asymptotics.gap_exceeds_twice_error_square` with the
admitted `T24_final … true` entries identity; the per-tape bounds use the per-word classifier
lemmas `selectedClassifier_yes_at` / `_no_at`; the error proof `decider_error_join_sq` is the
text of `decider_error_join` with the square header word (generated by `make_sq.py`).
`T24_square_class_effective_final` carries the square route-B assembly premise `hAsm`.

No ledger row is closed.
-/

noncomputable section

